WEBVTT

00:00:03.271 --> 00:00:07.743
Why isn't this dialing explains each queue or campaign that has work.

00:00:07.743 --> 00:00:12.216
A card shows how many records are pending, how many are dialable now,

00:00:12.216 --> 00:00:16.331
and how many are held back, then lists the reasons with counts.

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:20.459
Notes under the list say how the campaign is paced, how many agents

00:00:20.459 --> 00:00:23.868
are signed in, and what routing found the last time it looked.

00:00:23.868 --> 00:00:27.426
Here no agents are signed in, and routing found no agent a moment

00:00:27.426 --> 00:00:28.780
ago, with the reason.

00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:33.134
Reasons for a held back record include:

00:00:33.134 --> 00:00:38.153
Scheduled for later, Waiting out the retry delay, Out of attempts, No number

00:00:38.153 --> 00:00:43.355
to dial, Do not call, On the national do-not-call registry, Outside the calling

00:00:43.355 --> 00:00:47.640
window, Number not in service, and Abandonment rate cap reached.

00:00:48.390 --> 00:00:50.015
Others point at setup:

00:00:50.015 --> 00:00:54.660
The queue is turned off, The queue's business hours are closed, The dialer

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:58.840
profile is turned off, Not in the queue, so routing never sees it,

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:01.452
and Assigned to a user for manual work.

00:01:01.452 --> 00:01:05.574
A card is red when something is wrong, and amber when records are

00:01:05.574 --> 00:01:07.780
held back and none are dialable.

